# Shadcn Admin Dashboard Reference

Use this rule only when the user explicitly asks for it or manually attaches it to the task.

Reference template:

- GitHub: `https://github.com/bundui/shadcn-admin-dashboard-free`

## Intent

When this rule is active, build new UI features by referencing the matching page, pattern, or component from the template before designing from scratch.

## How to apply it

1. Identify whether the requested feature already exists in the template, either as a full page or as a reusable section.
2. Use the template as the primary visual and structural reference for layout, spacing, card composition, filters, tables, forms, tabs, drawers, and other shadcn-style patterns.
3. Adapt that pattern to this codebase's routing, data model, naming, state, and shared components instead of copying large template files verbatim.
4. Prefer existing local shadcn components first, then add missing pieces in the same style if the template uses something this app does not have yet.
5. Keep the implementation mobile-first and consistent with the rest of the app.

## Example

If the user asks for a calendar section and explicitly references this rule, inspect the template's calendar example and use that as the design and interaction baseline for the local implementation.

## Output expectation

When this rule is used, mention which template area informed the implementation so the user can see the mapping between the request and the chosen reference.
